On Dec 30, 8:44 am, "Boudewijn Waijers" <kroi...@home.nl> wrote:
> Next to that, there are monsters and non-player characters. The line
> between those is thin. For example, I wouldn't call a demon lord a
> monster, but rather a (non-player) character, but a simple ice devil
> would be a monster, even if it is intelligent.

The term "monster" in Nethack, and indeed most all RPGs, dates back to
original D&D, where it was a blanket term for all opponents --
animals, magical beasts, demons, constructs, even human beings.
Nethack's monsters have an unusual amount of personality, so both
"monster" and "NPC" terms could be seen to have meaning in all cases,
but monster is the traditional usage.

